WEBVTT

00:08:57.807 --> 00:09:00.232
and they feel like
they've achieved enough success,

00:09:00.256 --> 00:09:02.819
and so they may scale back a little bit.

00:09:02.843 --> 00:09:06.981
It may be that priorities outside of work
become more important to them.

00:09:07.005 --> 00:09:09.050
And if we can maintain that motivation,

00:09:09.074 --> 00:09:12.940
there's no inherent reason why the quality
of creative output would decline.

00:09:12.964 --> 00:09:14.169
What do you think?

00:09:14.193 --> 00:09:17.035
AB: Hmm, I'm willing
to entertain your hypothesis.

00:09:17.059 --> 00:09:18.257
AG: OK, cool.

00:09:18.281 --> 00:09:21.677
So there's a study I really like
of scientists, filmmakers and artists,

00:09:21.701 --> 00:09:24.129
showing that as they advance
from their 20s and 30s

00:09:24.153 --> 00:09:25.780
toward their 50s and 60s,

00:09:25.804 --> 00:09:27.756
they do less work.

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:29.867
The scientists run fewer experiments,

00:09:29.891 --> 00:09:32.318
the filmmakers don't make as many movies